# Build Script Maintenance Rule

The project ships as a single `dist/ContentUploader.exe` produced by `build_exe.bat` (PyInstaller). This rule keeps that build reproducible and self-contained.

## 1. Before finishing a task: review build_exe.bat

After ANY change that affects what gets shipped, check whether `build_exe.bat` (and `requirements.txt`) needs an update:

- Added a new `pip` package -> add it to `requirements.txt`. The `.bat` already runs `pip install -r requirements.txt`, no change needed there.
- Added a new runtime data file (icon, JSON config, fonts, sample assets, etc.) -> add a `--add-data "src;dst"` flag to the PyInstaller invocation in `build_exe.bat`.
- Added a new module that uses dynamic imports (e.g. plugins, sub-modules of PySide6/playwright/keyring) -> add `--collect-all <package>` or `--hidden-import <module>` to `build_exe.bat`.
- Added a new external binary dependency (browser, ffmpeg, etc.) that needs to be on the user's machine -> ensure either (a) it is installed by `build_exe.bat` (e.g. `playwright install`) and bundled into the exe, OR (b) the app downloads/installs it on first run. Anything the end user does not have on a clean Windows machine MUST be handled by `build_exe.bat` or by the app itself.

If anything needed an update, update `build_exe.bat` accordingly.

## 2. After finishing a task: run build_exe.bat

ALWAYS run `build_exe.bat` from the project root at the very end of any task that modified `.py` files, `requirements.txt`, or assets.

- Working directory: `c:\Users\Fearplay\Documents\CursorProjects\Content`
- Command: `cmd /c build_exe.bat` (or run the .bat directly)
- The build can take a few minutes - allow up to 10 minutes before assuming it hung.

## 3. Report the result

In the response to the user, include:
- Build success or failure.
- If failed: the last 20 lines of PyInstaller output.
- If succeeded: confirm `dist\ContentUploader.exe` exists and (optionally) its file size.

## What is NOT in scope

- Do not auto-build after every individual file edit during the task. Build only once, at the end.
- Do not commit `build/`, `dist/`, or `*.spec` - they are git-ignored and regenerated by every build.
